# CQ-24 · annotation-confidence
#
# Question: Which asserted triples does the corpus attach a producer confidence
#           to, and what is the value?
# Persona:  P1 — generation-pipeline engineer. A confidence per edge is what
#           makes a partially-trusted extraction usable: the gate says the
#           document is well-formed, and this says which edges the producer
#           itself was unsure of.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §5.11 (Annotation reification); §3.4
# Form:     SELECT — one row per annotated triple carrying a confidence
# Note:     This reads the RDF 1.1-portable `vso:Annotation` form only. §5.11
#           states the RDF-star quoted-triple form as the canonical equivalent;
#           CQ-29 is the same question written once across both forms, and it is
#           documented-future because no engine in this repository's dependency
#           set parses a quoted triple. That gap is a tooling fact, and naming
#           it here is the honest reading of "both forms are conformant".
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

SELECT ?doc ?subject ?predicate ?object ?confidence
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?doc {
    ?annotation a vso:Annotation ;
                vso:annotatedSubject   ?subject ;
                vso:annotatedPredicate ?predicate ;
                vso:annotatedObject    ?object ;
                vso:confidence         ?confidence .
  }
}
ORDER BY ?doc ?subject ?predicate
